      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $E=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find ${E}^{2}.$\n\n| ${E}^{2}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $1$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $5$ | {{field-3}} | $1$ |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} | $1$ | {{field-5}} |  |  |",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To find ${E}^{2},$ we multiply $E$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}^{2} & =E\\cdot E \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
