      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $F=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find ${F}^{3}.$\n\n| ${F}^{3}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, to find ${F}^{2},$ we multiply $F$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{2} & =F\\cdot F \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${F}^{3}={F}^{2}\\cdot F,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{3} & ={F}^{2}\\cdot F \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
